(56858, 2275, 'Q6858: A man says, "This boy is the son of the wife of my father." How is the boy related if he has no brothers?', 'Father', 'Brother', 'Son', 'Uncle', 'C', 1, 'Father\'s wife is his mother. Son of his mother is himself or brother. Since no brothers, he is his Son.', 8),
(56859, 2275, 'Q6859: A person walks 3728m North, turns right and walks 3733m East. Find distance from origin.', '5280 m East', '5271 m North', '5286 m SE', '5276 m NE', 'D', 1, 'Distance = √(3728² + 3733²) = 5276m NE.', 9),
(56860, 2275, 'Q6860: If South-East becomes North, North-East becomes West, what does West become?', 'South-West', 'North-East', 'South-East', 'North-West', 'A', 1, '135° anti-clockwise rotation turns West into South-East.', 10),
(56861, 2275, 'Q6861: What is the angle between clock hands at 2:00?', '75°', '60°', '50°', '90°', 'B', 1, 'Angle = 2 × 30° = 60°.', 11),
(56862, 2275, 'Q6862: If 1st Jan of a non-leap year is Friday, what day is 31st Dec of the same year?', 'Monday', 'Friday', 'Sunday', 'Saturday', 'C', 1, '365 days = 52 weeks + 1 day. 31st Dec is same day as 1st Jan = Friday.', 12),
(56863, 2275, 'Q6863: 5 people (A,B,C,D,E) sit in a row. C is in the middle. Where is C seated?', 'Extreme Left', 'Extreme Right', 'Immediate Right', 'Center / Middle', 'D', 1, 'C occupies 3rd position (Middle).', 13),
(56864, 2275, 'Q6864: In two parallel rows facing each other, A is opposite to X. How are A and X positioned?', 'Opposite to each other', 'Adjacent', 'Diagonal', 'Cannot determine', 'A', 1, 'A and X are seated directly opposite each other.', 14),
(56865, 2275, 'Q6865: 4 people sit around a circular table facing center. A is clockwise from B. B is to A\'s?', 'Immediate Right', 'Immediate Left', 'Opposite', 'Second to Right', 'B', 1, 'Facing center, clockwise means B is to the Immediate Left of A.', 15),
(56866, 2275, 'Q6866: In outward circular seating, left movement corresponds to clockwise rotation. Where are they facing?', 'Facing Center', 'Facing North', 'Facing Away from Center', 'Facing South', 'C', 1, 'Outward seating means facing away from center.', 16),
(56867, 2275, 'Q6867: Statements: All dogs are mammals. All mammals are animals. Conclusions: I. All dogs are animals. II. All animals are dogs.', 'Only Conclusion II follows', 'Both I and II follow', 'Neither follows', 'Only Conclusion I follows', 'D', 1, 'Dogs ⊂ Mammals ⊂ Animals. Conclusion I follows.', 17),
(56868, 2275, 'Q6868: Statements: No cats are dogs. No dogs are birds. Conclusions: I. No cats are birds. II. All birds are cats.', 'Neither follows', 'Only I follows', 'Only II follows', 'Both follow', 'A', 1, 'No direct relationship between cats and birds is established. Neither follows.', 18),
(56869, 2275, 'Q6869: Statement: "Drive carefully to avoid accidents." Conclusion I: Careless driving causes accidents.', 'Conclusion II is implicit', 'Conclusion I is implicit', 'Both implicit', 'Neither implicit', 'B', 1, 'The warning directly implies careless driving leads to accidents.', 19),
