(56963, 2279, 'Q6963: 5 people (A,B,C,D,E) sit in a row. C is in the middle. Where is C seated?', 'Extreme Left', 'Extreme Right', 'Immediate Right', 'Center / Middle', 'D', 1, 'C occupies 3rd position (Middle).', 13),
(56964, 2279, 'Q6964: In two parallel rows facing each other, A is opposite to X. How are A and X positioned?', 'Opposite to each other', 'Adjacent', 'Diagonal', 'Cannot determine', 'A', 1, 'A and X are seated directly opposite each other.', 14),
(56965, 2279, 'Q6965: 4 people sit around a circular table facing center. A is clockwise from B. B is to A\'s?', 'Immediate Right', 'Immediate Left', 'Opposite', 'Second to Right', 'B', 1, 'Facing center, clockwise means B is to the Immediate Left of A.', 15),
(56966, 2279, 'Q6966: In outward circular seating, left movement corresponds to clockwise rotation. Where are they facing?', 'Facing Center', 'Facing North', 'Facing Away from Center', 'Facing South', 'C', 1, 'Outward seating means facing away from center.', 16),
(56967, 2279, 'Q6967: Statements: All dogs are mammals. All mammals are animals. Conclusions: I. All dogs are animals. II. All animals are dogs.', 'Only Conclusion II follows', 'Both I and II follow', 'Neither follows', 'Only Conclusion I follows', 'D', 1, 'Dogs ⊂ Mammals ⊂ Animals. Conclusion I follows.', 17),
