(59955, 2399, 'Q9955: If "SMART" is coded as "VPDUW" under (+3) shift, how is it encoded?', 'WQEVX', 'UOCTV', 'XRFWY', 'VPDUW', 'D', 1, 'Shift each letter forward by +3.', 5),
(59956, 2399, 'Q9956: In a matrix code where X(n) = n × 7, evaluate X(4956).', '34692', '34696', '34687', '34702', 'A', 1, 'Result = 4956 × 7 = 34692.', 6),
(59957, 2399, 'Q9957: Pointing to a man, Priya says, "His mother is the only daughter of my mother." How is the man related to Priya?', 'Father', 'Brother', 'Grandfather', 'Sister', 'B', 1, 'Priya\'s mother\'s only daughter is Priya. Man is her son, making relation Brother.', 7),
(59958, 2399, 'Q9958: A man says, "This boy is the son of the wife of my father." How is the boy related if he has no brothers?', 'Father', 'Brother', 'Son', 'Uncle', 'C', 1, 'Father\'s wife is his mother. Son of his mother is himself or brother. Since no brothers, he is his Son.', 8),
(59959, 2399, 'Q9959: A person walks 9928m North, turns right and walks 9933m East. Find distance from origin.', '14048 m East', '14039 m North', '14054 m SE', '14044 m NE', 'D', 1, 'Distance = √(9928² + 9933²) = 14044m NE.', 9),
(59960, 2399, 'Q9960: If South-East becomes North, North-East becomes West, what does West become?', 'South-West', 'North-East', 'South-East', 'North-West', 'A', 1, '135° anti-clockwise rotation turns West into South-East.', 10),
(59961, 2399, 'Q9961: What is the angle between clock hands at 6:00?', '195°', '180°', '170°', '210°', 'B', 1, 'Angle = 6 × 30° = 180°.', 11),
(59962, 2399, 'Q9962: If 1st Jan of a non-leap year is Friday, what day is 31st Dec of the same year?', 'Monday', 'Friday', 'Sunday', 'Saturday', 'C', 1, '365 days = 52 weeks + 1 day. 31st Dec is same day as 1st Jan = Friday.', 12),
(59963, 2399, 'Q9963: 5 people (A,B,C,D,E) sit in a row. C is in the middle. Where is C seated?', 'Extreme Left', 'Extreme Right', 'Immediate Right', 'Center / Middle', 'D', 1, 'C occupies 3rd position (Middle).', 13),
(59964, 2399, 'Q9964: In two parallel rows facing each other, A is opposite to X. How are A and X positioned?', 'Opposite to each other', 'Adjacent', 'Diagonal', 'Cannot determine', 'A', 1, 'A and X are seated directly opposite each other.', 14),
(59965, 2399, 'Q9965: 4 people sit around a circular table facing center. A is clockwise from B. B is to A\'s?', 'Immediate Right', 'Immediate Left', 'Opposite', 'Second to Right', 'B', 1, 'Facing center, clockwise means B is to the Immediate Left of A.', 15),
(59966, 2399, 'Q9966: In outward circular seating, left movement corresponds to clockwise rotation. Where are they facing?', 'Facing Center', 'Facing North', 'Facing Away from Center', 'Facing South', 'C', 1, 'Outward seating means facing away from center.', 16),
(59967, 2399, 'Q9967: Statements: All dogs are mammals. All mammals are animals. Conclusions: I. All dogs are animals. II. All animals are dogs.', 'Only Conclusion II follows', 'Both I and II follow', 'Neither follows', 'Only Conclusion I follows', 'D', 1, 'Dogs ⊂ Mammals ⊂ Animals. Conclusion I follows.', 17),
(59968, 2399, 'Q9968: Statements: No cats are dogs. No dogs are birds. Conclusions: I. No cats are birds. II. All birds are cats.', 'Neither follows', 'Only I follows', 'Only II follows', 'Both follow', 'A', 1, 'No direct relationship between cats and birds is established. Neither follows.', 18),
(59969, 2399, 'Q9969: Statement: "Drive carefully to avoid accidents." Conclusion I: Careless driving causes accidents.', 'Conclusion II is implicit', 'Conclusion I is implicit', 'Both implicit', 'Neither implicit', 'B', 1, 'The warning directly implies careless driving leads to accidents.', 19),
(59970, 2399, 'Q9970: Statement: "Please post this letter." Assumption I: The letter will reach its destination via post.', 'Assumption II is implicit', 'Both implicit', 'Assumption I is implicit', 'Neither implicit', 'C', 1, 'The request assumes the postal service will deliver the letter.', 20),
(59971, 2399, 'Q9971: Is X an even integer? Statement I: X is divisible by 4. Statement II: X > 10.', 'Statement II alone is sufficient', 'Both statements together needed', 'Neither is sufficient', 'Statement I alone is sufficient', 'D', 1, 'Statement I alone proves X is even because any multiple of 4 is even.', 21),
(59972, 2399, 'Q9972: In a class of 30 students, Rahul ranks 7th from top. What is his rank from bottom?', '24th', '26th', '21th', '29th', 'A', 1, 'Rank from bottom = (Total - Rank from top + 1) = (30 - 7 + 1) = 24th.', 22),
(59973, 2399, 'Q9973: Select a 3-member team from A,B,C,D where A must be with B, and B with C.', 'Group {A, D, E}', 'Group {A, B, C}', 'Group {B, C, D}', 'Group {C, E, F}', 'B', 1, 'Team must include A, B, and C together.', 23),
(59974, 2399, 'Q9974: In a 5-story building, A lives on floor 5. Which floor does A occupy?', 'Floor 6', 'Floor 4', 'Floor 5', 'Floor 7', 'C', 1, 'A occupies Floor 5.', 24),
(59975, 2399, 'Q9975: Meeting is scheduled on the first working day of the week. Which day is it?', 'Tuesday', 'Wednesday', 'Thursday', 'Monday', 'D', 1, 'First working day of standard week is Monday.', 25),
