(66101, 2645, 'Q16101: [C/C++ Pointers] What is the size of a pointer in a 64-bit operating system?', '4 bytes', '8 bytes', '2 bytes', '16 bytes', 'B', 1, 'On a 64-bit OS, memory addresses are 64 bits = 8 bytes long.', 1),
(66102, 2645, 'Q16102: [C/C++ Output] Which operator is used to access members of a structure through a pointer in C?', '.', '*', '->', '&', 'C', 1, 'The arrow operator `->` dereferences and accesses structure members.', 2),
(66103, 2645, 'Q16103: [Java OOPs] Which Java keyword prevents a class from being subclassed / inherited?', 'static', 'abstract', 'private', 'final', 'D', 1, 'The "final" keyword applied to a class prevents inheritance.', 3),
(66104, 2645, 'Q16104: [Java Polymorphism] What is Method Overloading in Java?', 'Same method name with different parameters in same class', 'Same method in child class with same signature', 'Method returning multiple values', 'Private method overriding', 'A', 1, 'Method overloading occurs when methods share name but have different parameter lists.', 4),
(66105, 2645, 'Q16105: [Data Structures - Arrays] What is the time complexity of accessing an element in an array by index?', 'O(n)', 'O(1)', 'O(log n)', 'O(n²)', 'B', 1, 'Arrays provide constant O(1) random access by index via base address calculation.', 5),
(66106, 2645, 'Q16106: [Data Structures - Linked List] In a singly linked list, what is the time complexity to insert a node at the head?', 'O(n)', 'O(log n)', 'O(1)', 'O(n²)', 'C', 1, 'Inserting at head requires updating head pointer, taking O(1) time.', 6),
